# Every tick

Run the ready queue. Act on the first Issue that can move. Never report
"nothing to do" while any step found work (#5012 / #5383 / #5408).

1. Inbound communication checkpoint, then `~/.cursor/lgfc-ready-queue.txt`.
2. Queue order: Operations interrupts, own exceptions, assigned ready or
   active, unclaimed ready, then unassigned primary or secondary.
3. Skip any `wait:*` after recording the blocker; take the next item.
4. One-line end report must name Issues or PRs touched or skipped **and**
   Operations Issues seen from queries 1 and 5 (not only Cursor-claimed).

## Split gated tasks

When a Production Go or other approval is missing for only part of a task,
do the part that needs none, record the held part, and label only that
held Issue `wait:*`. Do not park the whole task on one wait label.

## Classify Operations on first pass

An unclassified open `team:operations` Issue gets an `ops:priority:N` from
the Operations holder on the first pass of a tick.

Law: `docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md` (Assigned-queue continuation).
Mechanics: `docs/ops/ai/CURSOR-RULES.md`; contract: ready-queue contract.
